  "title": "Week 33: View Transition ✨",
  "date": "2023-08-19T21:00:00.000Z",
  "content": "Week 33: View Transition ✨\n\nWeb Components 🧩\n\nI’ve been looking into Lit — it’s a pretty neat library for building web components. If you’re using TypeScript, you’ll need decorators to get the most out of it.\n\nView Transitions 🎞️\n\nAstro.js now supports View Transitions. It’s a slick way to animate block elements between pages, giving your site a smoother, app-like feel.\n\n3D Stuff 🕶️\n\nd.design → Alibaba’s 3D modeling site, worth checking out!\n\nOGL → a lightweight 3D rendering library that’s super clean and minimal.\n\nGermany 🇩🇪\n\nFound DAAD — a great resource if you’re considering studying in Germany.\n\nThailand 🇹🇭\n\nIf you’re up for learning Thai, Duke Language School in Thailand looks like a solid option.",
